  "request": "Second-cycle floor not clickable; rhythm INPUT_TIME under latency; additional report: refresh before every attempt avoids a black MEMORY screen.",
  "findings": {
    "floor": "Each MEMORY replaces its buttons, but the projection cache only considered camera/viewport. Round 2 reused the cache and left all 30 new hit targets unsized.",
    "input": "Serialized action acknowledgements blocked later key delivery. A 1,800ms acknowledgement delay reproduced the exact INPUT_TIME toast and scored only 1 of 8 centered inputs.",
    "blackScreen": "Retry in the same iframe after a failed run reproduced a blank MEMORY canvas (0/30 outlines) and null alphaMode exception. V3 correctly retired the boss idle texture; Nox retained that destroyed Texture in a module cache and reused it. The earlier renderer-resume fix did not clear these art references.",
    "priorCoverageGap": "Earlier reentry tests closed/reopened the iframe and stopped at round-2 RHYTHM. They did not test a same-document retry or round-2 MEMORY hit areas."
  },
  "changes": {
    "floor": "Projection cache also tracks challenge and new button identity. Neutral cyan diamond before input; gold numbered marks only after accepted steps. No rule or tile-count changes.",
    "input": "Bounded (8 in flight) cumulative input stream sends keys without waiting for an earlier response. Server applies only the unacknowledged suffix, using its existing atomic per-member sequence guard. Retries preserve packet content; responses cannot regress committed room revision. Clock samples include error responses. Retry backoff and phase/exit aborts bound unfinished work.",
    "art": "Per-battle Nox art references clear at teardown; 48 derived frame textures retire without double-destroying source images. All 9 source images join the existing V3 release lifecycle. Cancelled preparation cannot restore old references.",
    "packaging": "The first staging attempt exceeded the Pages 20,000-file cap by one. The new art helper is already compiled into the renderer and remains in Git; exclude only its unused separate public copy. Include the generated historical archive in the asset-count regression.",
    "cache": "input4 HTML/module/bundle keys; client version 3 blocks starting new rooms with response-blocking clients. Existing legacy action packets retain their replay checks."
  },
